<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    HTTP error pages — the Odoo-rendered 404.

    This is the page Odoo itself serves for an unknown route (http_routing.404,
    rendered through web.frontend_layout).  It is NOT nginx's 404, which never
    reaches Odoo at all — nginx answers /web/database/* and its own static
    misses directly, and that page lives in nginx/nginx.conf.template.  A demo
    visitor who mistypes a URL lands here, so it is a brand surface.

    Stock content (odoo/addons/http_routing/views/http_routing_template.xml:119)
    is an English "We couldn't find the page you're looking for!" next to Odoo's
    own purple 404 illustration, plus a "popular pages" block that lists exactly
    one link because no website pages exist on this build.

    ⚠ WHY THE COPY IS FRENCH IN THE SOURCE AND NOT IN i18n/fr.po.
    The module convention is English source + fr.po, and that is correct for
    every string this module renders through the ORM — but it only works if a
    French language is ACTIVE.  On this build it is not: res_lang has en_US and
    nothing else, and neither entrypoint.sh nor any provisioning module ever
    installs fr_FR.  Odoo also resolves the language for an anonymous frontend
    request from the website/default language, not from the visitor's browser,
    so even loading fr_FR would not by itself make this page French for a
    prospect.  Translating via fr.po would therefore have produced a msgstr
    nothing ever reads, and the page would have stayed in English.

    If fr_FR is ever installed and made the default, this text is already the
    wanted output — nothing here needs undoing, but the en_US rendering of the
    page becomes French too.  That is the deliberate trade.

    ⚠ WHY THE LOGO IS static/description/brand/logo_methode.svg AND NOT A NEW
    ASSET.  It is the same mark as the brand's current export (the 694x633 one
    is the identical geometry with ~170px of empty canvas below it), and it is
    already the file the login page serves — see login_templates.xml, including
    why res.company.logo cannot hold an SVG.  Adding a second copy would give
    the mark two sources of truth for no visual difference.
-->
<odoo>

    <template id="error_404_brand" inherit_id="http_routing.404">
        <!--
            Anchored on the oe_structure's section rather than on the
            oe_structure div itself: with the website module installed that div
            is an editable drop zone whose id Odoo uses to key stored edits, so
            replacing the div would take the zone away with it.  website is not
            installed on this build, and this xpath keeps that from mattering.
        -->
        <xpath expr="//div[hasclass('oe_structure')]/section" position="replace">
            <section class="m-error-page">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="m-error-page__card text-center">
                        <!--
                            ⚠ The inline max-height is deliberate, and mirrors
                            login_templates.xml.  logo_methode.svg carries
                            width="700" height="700", so if this element ever
                            paints before web.assets_frontend is available it
                            renders 700px tall and shoves the copy off screen.
                            The sizing constraint travels with the element;
                            refinements live in error_pages.scss.
                        -->
                        <img src="/methode_theme/static/description/brand/logo_methode.svg"
                             alt="Méthode"
                             class="m-error-page__logo"
                             style="max-height:140px; max-width:100%; width:auto"/>

                        <p class="m-error-page__code">Erreur 404</p>
                        <h1 class="m-error-page__title">Cette page n’existe pas</h1>
                        <p class="m-error-page__lead">
                            L’adresse est peut-être incorrecte, ou la page a été
                            déplacée ou supprimée.
                        </p>

                        <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg m-error-page__action">
                            Retour à l’accueil
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>
        </xpath>
    </template>

</odoo>
